@startbpmn BP02_MaintainLifeThemes
lang en             ' the only stakeholder is the Software Architect, who authored the sources in English

output L1 "01_detailed/BP02_MaintainLifeThemes.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP02_MaintainLifeThemes.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - a theme is never archivable, only deleted or kept: BR-23
'   - the theme deletion offers two cascades, its goals and its ideas: BR-13, SA 2026-10-13
'   - a goal cannot be kept theme-less, so declining is not offered there: BR-21, BR-01
'   - a routine has NO theme, so a theme deletion never reaches one and the routines cascade -
'     with the declinable occurrence cascade under it - is gone: BR-02, BR-13, SA 2026-10-13
'   - an idea kept through the cascade simply becomes theme-less: BR-03
'   - every cascade the user may legally decline is off by default: BR-19
'   - WHICH cascades the gesture offers, and in which order the user answers them, is not
'     business relevant: the drawing carries one choice - a valid combination, or no deletion -
'     and what the combinations are is the disclosure's content (BP02.05): SA 2026-10-11
'   - an act does not send the user back to re-reading the tab: every act returns to the tab they
'     are working, where the next one is chosen, and the surface is current without anyone asking
'     for it: BR-118, SA 2026-10-11
'   - the deletion discloses what it will take before it takes it: BR-12
'   - the starter set is Health / Career / Learning / Relationships / Personal, and it ships with
'     the template files installed when the data folder is created: BR-82, QB-08, SA 2026-10-10
'   - there is NO restoring that set: a user who wants the shipped folder back deletes the folder
'     and starts from scratch, outside Bearing. BR-83 is VOID and call site BP02.09 is RETIRED,
'     its id never reused: SA 2026-10-11 ("I don't see a need to reset the data directory")
'   - the overview counts active goals only; routines are not on this view: BR-95, BR-02
'   - the overview reads one surface whole - themes, vision, mission, goals and measures - and
'     reports what it collected: SA 2026-10-11, SA 2026-10-13
'   - the answer to that read IS drawn, and it has to be: the gateway decides what needs doing
'     ON that data, so without it the user is deciding in front of an empty tab. What was wrong
'     was the LABEL - "The themes overview" repeated the request's own words, so the two arrows
'     read as one thing and understated what comes back; the reply names the payload instead:
'     SA 2026-10-11
'   - the theme name drafts as it is typed like any draftable field, and the operation that keeps
'     it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not here: BR-121 is a bound rule on the editor step. Call site
'     BP02.10 (Draft the theme input) is RETIRED, its id never reused: SA 2026-10-11
'   - colour propagates from the theme downstream: BR-09
'   - vision and mission are optional prose above themes, reset by emptying: section 3
'   - one editor per entity serves creating and editing alike, so the whole gesture is ONE editor
'     box, ONE submit box and ONE request: UX-04. What separated creating from amending was the
'     placement of a new theme in the order, and that is not business relevant, so the two chains
'     are one and the case never has to be asked. Call site BP02.03 (Amend a theme) is RETIRED,
'     its id never reused, and BP02.02 is the one editing request: SA 2026-10-11
'   - where a new theme lands in the order is not drawn: the user orders them when they want to
'     (BP02.04), which is the business fact: SA 2026-10-11
'   - showing that editor is the UI's doing and asks the system for nothing, so no step draws it;
'     which dialog it is lives in Intent section 7's surface inventory: SA 2026-10-11
'   - expanding or collapsing a section is handled entirely in the UI and asks the system for
'     nothing, so it is NOT a step in a business process: SA 2026-10-11 (the same holds for any
'     future fold/unfold)
'   - the overview reads this surface WHOLE, so expanding the vision and mission section has
'     nothing left to fetch: call site BP02.07 (Read vision and mission) is RETIRED and its id is
'     never reused: SA 2026-10-11, ADR-066
'   - a step never enumerates the fields a request stores: which fields the entity carries is
'     a Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step names the act and its subject
'     only: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user NAMES a life area -
'     colour is a field of that same editor - and STATES a vision and a mission. Edit stays the
'     operation's word and the call sites keep their ids: BR-82, BR-09, ADR-066, SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'
' Call-site collapsing (ADR-069, design-artifact-conventions): rename and recolour are two
' variations of one amend request, not two chains - the variation is a permutation of the
' operation, discovered at Design, and never a second call site here. The cross-process duplication
' this comment used to flag is GONE: BP01's onboarding wizard was retired on 2026-10-11, so
' recording a vision and a mission happens here and nowhere else.

' ===== The user: opens the Themes tab and performs one act =====
pool "User" {
  start "A theme needs attention"
  :Work a theme;
  rule BR-118

  if "What needs doing?" then "add or change a theme"
    :Name the theme;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the theme;
    send "Edit a theme" to editIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as recorded
    end "Theme recorded"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "reorder them"
    :Order a theme;
    send "Reorder themes" to reorderIn
    receive "The ordering outcome" as reordered
    end "Themes ordered"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "retire one for good"
    :Delete a theme;
    send "See what deleting a theme takes" to impactIn
    receive "What the deletion will take" as impact
    if "Approve what the deletion takes?" rule BR-13 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      rule BR-21
      :Confirm the deletion;
      send "Delete a theme" to deleteIn
      receive "The deletion outcome" as deleted
      note "A kept idea loses only its theme affiliation. The goals cannot be kept, so confirming takes them."
    else "reject"
      end "Deletion abandoned"
    endif
    end "Theme deleted"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "state who I want to become, and what I am here for"
    :State the vision and mission;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the vision and mission;
    send "Record vision and mission" to vmIn
    receive "The recording outcome" as vmDone
    end "Vision and mission recorded"
  endif
}

' ===== The system: one chain per request, each a single synchronous call =====
system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Theme submitted" as editIn
  call "BP02.02_EditTheme" "Edit a theme" {
    :Store the edit;
    rule BR-09
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to recorded
  end "Theme answered"

  messageStart "Theme reordering requested" as reorderIn
  call "BP02.04_ReorderThemes" "Reorder themes" {
    :Apply the new order;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The ordering outcome" to reordered
  end "Reordering answered"

  messageStart "Deletion impact requested" as impactIn
  call "BP02.05_ReadTheDeletionImpact" "See what deleting a theme takes" {
    :Report what the deletion will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-12
    rule BR-13
    rule BR-14
    rule BR-15
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-21
    rule BR-117
  }
  send "What the deletion will take" to impact
  note "A goal requires a theme, so keeping one is not a legal outcome: where the theme has goals the gesture is approve-or-abandon. An idea may stay behind theme-less, so that cascade is the real choice and it starts off. An archived descendant is counted like a live one."
  end "Impact answered"

  messageStart "Theme deletion requested" as deleteIn
  call "BP02.06_DeleteTheme" "Delete a theme" {
    :Delete confirmed items;
    rule BR-03
    rule BR-13
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The deletion outcome" to deleted
  note "The request carries the cascades the user confirmed, and nothing else goes: an idea left out stays, theme-less. What happens below a deleted goal or idea is that entity's own rule, applied where the deletion reaches it."
  end "Deletion answered"

  messageStart "Vision and mission submitted" as vmIn
  call "BP02.08_RecordVisionAndMission" "Record vision and mission" {
    :Store the vision and the mission;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The recording outcome" to vmDone
  end "Record answered"
}

@endbpmn
